WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.180
Hey this is Presh Talwalkar! Can you figure out a pattern in these numbers?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.520
This intelligence test has been shared on Facebook more than 3 million times.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.300
It's also gotten popular on Twitter

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.080
with the tagline that if you understand it,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.340
you have the genius IQ of more than 150 points.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.880
There are many reasons to question these claims,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.860
and perhaps the most startling part about this intelligence test,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.380
is that you never have to prove you understand the rule.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.700
You can simply pretend you solved it by sharing the post or sharing the tweet.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.300
I often get people who watch my puzzle videos and tell me that it was so easy, they figured it out.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.220
When I ask them what the answer is,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.180
they often tell me a result which is the trap answer.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.980
I think in order to have an intelligence test,

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:01.620
You should always prove that you understand what is going on in a new situation.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.580
So, I want to pose this problem to you,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.000
If you understand the rule, you should be able to solve this problem.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.900
Give it a try and when you are ready, keep watching the video, I'm going to explain the rule of the intelligence test and then solve this problem.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.920
So, when we are looking for patterns in these numbers,

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.000
we might just start by adding up the numbers and seeing if these numbers show up anywhere.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:32.820
In fact, it turns out that the sum of the two digits will be the last two digits or the last digit in our result.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.940
Now we need to figure out where the first number, or the first two numbers of our answer comes from.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:45.500
While we can do the other operation, we can just subtract the numbers and we will quickly see that this is the first number or the first

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.500
two numbers come from.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.840
So, we figured out the intelligence rule.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.280
We want to add, combine two numbers, x and y

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.980
we'll take the difference of the two numbers

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.540
and then append it to the sum of the two numbers.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.200
So now let's test our knowledge and see if we can solve a new problem.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.920
One way we can interpret this problem is that we want two numbers to combine

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:13.080
so that the two numbers have a difference of one, and a sum of 23.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.800
We have a system with 2 equations and x and y

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.640
If we add up these 2 equations, we can eliminate  the y variable

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.320
So we have 2x equals 24, which we then solve that x is equal to 12.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.620
y will be 1 less than that, so y equals 11.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.940
So we figured out 12 and 11 combine to be 123.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:40.060
But if we were to truly have an intelligence test, we need to look for all solutions.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.800
There is another way we can interpret our problem.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:49.240
We could have two numbers combine so they have a difference of 12, and a sum of 3.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:58.500
We can solve these equations similarly, and we will get that x is equal to 7 and a half, and y is equal to negative 4 and a half.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.460
So this is another answer to this new problem I've suggested.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:13.680
I would say, this is a little bit more of an intelligence test than the original problem. And now I'm going to ask you, share this video if you solved this new problem.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.020
Be honest.

